{"rule_id": "MET_DOC_WORKFLOW_V5_1", "path": "IC/README.md", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 10, "excerpt": "Degree Discount Algorithm
-------------------------

Degree discount heuristic was proposed first by [Chen et al.](http://snap.stanford.edu/class/cs224w-readings/chen09influence.pdf) (Algorithm 4) Its results are slightly inferior than greedy hill-climbing algorithms, however it runs several orders of magnitudes faster. It's fine-tuned for Independent Cascade model. Running time is O(k*log(n)+m), where k - number of initial targets, n - number of vertices, m - number of edges. ", "matched_conditions": ["algorithm", "proposed"], "supporting_conditions": [], "documentation_dimensions": {"activity": "algorithm", "object": "proposed", "context": "research", "polarity": "affirmative", "scope": "repository", "layer": "contextual", "heading": "influence maximization in social graphs / degree discount algorithm", "unit_version": "documented-workflow-v5"}, "exclusion_reasons": [], "excerpt_sha256": "a64dea14a496e4eb8802867bc61da2cd7a5fc5d3375d5275657eff9862493fc8"}

